//prsindia.org/billtrack/the-electricity-amendment-bill-2022"]],domain:"grid"},{what:"PFCCL's ten empanelled AMISPs (17 Mar 2025) — names are in an image and were not extracted.",whyItMatters:"Empanelment defines the eligible field for ~Rs 1 lakh crore of metering; the list is the denominator for any AMISP concentration claim.",srcs:[["T&D India, 17 Mar 2025: PFCCL empanels ten AMISPs for smart metering projects under RDSS","https://www.tndindia.com/pfccl-empanels-ten-amisps-for-smart-metering-projects-under-rdss/"]],domain:"grid"},{what:"Market coupling operator design: CERC's Jul 2025 order has exchanges rotating as MCO with Grid-India as backup; Powerline (Jul 2026) describes Grid-India as the appointed MCO. The 2026 draft/final regulations were not opened.",whyItMatters:"Whether a PSU or the exchanges run coupling changes who captures fees and data.",srcs:[["Power Peak Digest, 24 Jul 2025: CERC sets phased timeline for market coupling rollout starting January 2026 (Petition 8/SM/2025)","https://powerpeakdigest.com/cerc-sets-phased-timeline-for-market-coupling-rollout-starting-january-2026/"],["Powerline, 3 Jul 2026: Unlocking efficiency — building a unified power market through market coupling","https://powerline.net.in/2026/07/17/unlocking-efficiency-building-a-unified-power-market-through-market-coupling-2"]],domain:"grid"},{what:"No opened official record names the private developers who previously held the 12 Arunachal projects re-allotted on 12 Aug 2023; PIB says only 'allotted to private sector developers about 15 years ago', SJVN's Etalin page names no prior developer, and the Dy CM's 2022 statement on 44 terminations names none.",whyItMatters:"Without the list, the exit terms of Jindal/GMR/Jaypee-type developers (compensation, forfeited premiums, litigation) cannot be compared with Reliance Power's priced Rs 128.39 cr exit.",srcs:[["PIB 12 Aug 2023: 12 stalled Arunachal hydro projects (11,517 MW) handed to hydro PSUs — project list, CPSU split, 'earlier allotted to private developers ~15 years ago'","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1948139"],["SJVN project page: Etalin HEP 3,097 MW — MoP allocation 22 Dec 2021, state allotment 21 Jul 2023, MoA 12 Aug 2023, EC obtained, DPR validity to 31 Dec 2024, investment-approval proposal to MoP 1 Mar 2024","https://sjvn.nic.in/en/etalin-hep"],["Arunachal Times 17 Mar 2022: Dy CM Chowna Mein tells assembly 44 MoAs with private developers terminated; 153 MoAs for 46,943 MW originally signed; developers not named","https://archive.arunachaltimes.in/index.php/2022/03/17/arunachal-govt-has-terminated-agreements-with-44-private-power-developers-dy-cm/"],["Business Standard/PTI 1 Jan 2024: Reliance Power to sell 1,200 MW Kalai-II development rights to THDC for Rs 128.39 cr; agreement 30 Dec 2023 with Governor of Arunachal Pradesh (regulatory filing)","https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/reliance-power-to-sell-1-200-mw-kalai-ii-hydropower-project-to-thdc-india-124010100410_1.html"]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"Neither outlet covering the 22 May 2025 CBI chargesheet carried any response from Patel Engineering Ltd, and no exchange filing by the company on the chargesheet was located.",whyItMatters:"The contradiction invariant requires the accused party's position; a listed company's silence on a chargesheet is itself notable.",srcs:[["Business Standard 22 May 2025: CBI chargesheets Satyapal Malik and five others (incl. Patel Engineering Ltd, ex-CVPPPL chairman Navin Kumar Choudhary) over Rs 2,200 cr Kiru civil-works contract; Malik denies","https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cbi-charges-former-j-k-governor-satyapal-malik-in-kiru-hydropower-case-125052201398_1.html"],["The Tribune May 2025: CBI chargesheet in Kiru case — FIR 2022, 47th CVPPPL board decision to re-tender via e-tender/reverse auction not implemented, award to Patel Engineering; Malik's Rs 300 cr bribe-offer claim and response","https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/j-k/cbi-files-chargesheet-against-former-j-k-governor-satyapal-malik-in-kiru-hydropower-corruption-case"]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"The Ratle turnkey contract value is absent from the signing coverage (Kashmir Life) and the Wikipedia summary; only the PIB investment recommendation (~Rs 5,282 cr, Sep 2020) is public.",whyItMatters:"MEIL's largest hydro EPC award cannot be sized or benchmarked against Polavaram.",srcs:[["Kashmir Life 11 Apr 2022: RHPCL and MEIL sign turnkey contract for 850 MW Ratle HEP (value not stated)","https://kashmirlife.net/ratle-project-rhpcl-meil-ink-contract-for-turnkey-execution-290251/"],["Wikipedia: Ratle Hydroelectric Plant — GVK 2013 BOOT award and exit, NHPC–J&K MoU Feb 2019, PIB investment approval ~Rs 5,282 cr Sep 2020, MEIL EPC, 21% complete May 2025","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratle_Hydroelectric_Plant"]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"No competitive process, bidder list or price is reported for AP's Gandikota-2 allocation to Adani Hydro Energy Eleven (May 2026) or Maharashtra's 2023 MoUs with Torrent and NHPC.",whyItMatters:"The 2024 enabling-infrastructure scheme pays central grants only to private projects 'allotted on a transparent basis'; absence of a process record leaves eligibility undetermined.",srcs:[["Business Standard 20 May 2026: AP SIPB (chaired by CM Naidu) approves allocation of 2,250 MW Gandikota-2 PSP to Adani Hydro Energy Eleven under AP Integrated Clean Energy Policy 2024; 72 months; 29.20 MCM water allocation","https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/adani-green-to-develop-2-250-mw-gandikota-2-pumped-storage-project-in-ap-126052000325_1.html"],["Deccan Herald 7 Jun 2023: Torrent Power MoU with Government of Maharashtra for three PSPs of 5,700 MW (Karjat 3,000, Maval 1,200, Junnar 1,500), ~Rs 27,000 cr, sites identified by Torrent, off-stream","https://www.deccanherald.com/national/west/torrent-inks-mega-power-deal-with-maharashtra-1225620.html"],["Deccan Herald 7 Jun 2023: NHPC MoU with Maharashtra for four PSPs totalling 7,350 MW (Kalu, Savitri, Jalond, Kengadi), signed in presence of Dy CM Fadnavis","https://www.deccanherald.com/amp/story/india%2Fnhpc-inks-mou-with-maharashtra-1225664.html"],["PIB 11 Sep 2024: Cabinet approves modified scheme of budgetary support for enabling infrastructure for HEPs — Rs 12,461 cr, 31,350 MW, FY25–FY32, eligibility incl. private and PSPs allotted transparently","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2053886"]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"No cash consideration to the Sikkim exchequer is reported for the transfer of the 60.08% Sikkim Urja stake; the only stated terms are assumption of Rs 3,079.74 cr dues and 6%→15% free power over 50 years.",whyItMatters:"A company with Rs 1,207 cr FY23 revenue and Rs 3,500 cr receivables was transferred for non-cash terms; the valuation basis is undisclosed.",srcs:[["Mongabay India Mar 2025: Sikkim cabinet 3 Feb 2024 divests 60.08% of Sikkim Urja to Greenko Energies; Rs 3,079.74 cr dues transferred; 6%→15% free power over 50 years; Rs 4,000 cr revival; EAC approval 10 Jan 2025; petitions by Tseten Tashi Bhutia (BJP) 24 Feb 2025 and M.K. Subba (ex-SDF); CM Tamang 'debt-free'","https://india.mongabay.com/2025/03/disinvestment-from-dam-challenged-in-court-in-fragile-himalayan-state/"],["ThePrint 12 Oct 2023: Teesta-III cost Rs 13,965 cr (vs Rs 5,705 cr 2005), shareholding SPICL 60.08%/Greenko Mauritius 35%/PTC 5%, lenders PFC/REC/SBI >Rs 10,000 cr, IFFCO-Tokio lead insurer, Athena→Greenko 2019, state stake 26%→60.08% in 2015","https://theprint.in/india/flood-submerged-teesta-iii-hydropower-plant-but-sikkim-govt-operator-still-owe-lenders-rs-10000-cr/1800822/"]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"No electoral-bond purchase by NCC Ltd, THDC's or NHPC's Tehri/Subansiri contractors was checked; L&T's and HCC's bond records were not opened (a press summary that L&T bought none was seen only in search results).",whyItMatters:"The money-trail across hydro contractors is partial: MEIL, Navayuga and Patel Engineering are recorded; the largest listed contractor (L&T) is not.",srcs:[["myneta.info (ADR) electoral-bond donor page: Patel Engineering Ltd Rs 6 cr, all to BJP","https://myneta.info/electoral_bonds/donor.php?donor=PATEL+ENGINEERING+LTD."]],domain:"hydro"},{what:"No court, SEBI, CAG or ED record was found that finds the Adani Group to be a proxy, front or financing vehicle for the BJP; the only primary records are allegations by opposition leaders and denials by both parties.",whyItMatters:"The most-circulated narrative in this domain rests entirely on inference from outcomes (growth, awards, access), not on any documented flow of money or control.",srcs:[["Wikipedia — Gautam Adani","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gautam_Adani"],["Wikipedia — Adani Group","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adani_Group"],["Indian Kanoon — Vishal Tiwari v Union of India, SC, 2024-01-03","https://indiankanoon.org/doc/188573380/"]],domain:"literature"},{what:"The March 2024 electoral-bond disclosures, as summarised, contain no documented link between any bond purchase and a specific coal block or energy contract.",whyItMatters:'The "pay-to-play for coal blocks" narrative needs a dated donation→award sequence; none was located.',srcs:[["Wikipedia — Electoral bond","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_bond"]],domain:"literature"},{what:"No Comptroller and Auditor General audit of PM CARES exists; the fund is audited privately and donor identities are undisclosed.",whyItMatters:'A documented absence of independent audit is a finding in its own right; it also means the "slush fund" narrative cannot be tested with public records.',srcs:[["Wikipedia — PM CARES Fund","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PM_CARES_Fund"]],domain:"literature"},{what:"The PRS listing of Standing Committee on Energy reports (2019–26) contains no report, by title, on the 2022 coal-import blending mandate or on the SECI manufacturing-linked solar tender.",whyItMatters:"Two of the decisions most often alleged to have favoured a single group have no located parliamentary-committee scrutiny.",srcs:[["PRS Legislative Research — Standing Committee report summaries","https://prsindia.org/policy/report-summaries"]],domain:"literature"},{what:"No Adani Group denial of the OCCRP (2023) or FT coal-grade (2024) reports was captured in the sources opened; the SEBI September 2025 final orders were not opened (sebi.gov.in returned 403).",whyItMatters:"Three of the key contradiction records for this file are missing on our side, not necessarily on theirs; the alleged claims here are therefore weaker than they should be.",srcs:[["Wikipedia — Adani Group","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adani_Group"]],domain:"literature"},{what:`Wikipedia's "Solar power in India" article contains no material on ALMM, the April 2022 customs duties or domestic manufacturers; MNRE/Mercom pages were not opened.`,whyItMatters:"The ALMM narratives below rest on general knowledge rather than opened primary notifications and are marked accordingly.",srcs:[["Wikipedia — Solar power in India","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_power_in_India"]],domain:"literature"},{what:"India's most publicised lithium discovery (Salal-Haimna, Reasi, J&K) has drawn no bid in two auction attempts (Tranche I: fewer than three qualified bidders; Tranche III: no bid at all), per the minister's Rajya Sabha reply of 2025-03-10.",whyItMatters:"The critical-minerals programme's flagship asset has no private taker; the deposit is explored only to G3 level. The narrative of lithium self-reliance rests on a block nobody would buy.",srcs:[["The Tribune, 10 Mar 2025","https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/j-k/reasi-lithium-block-auction-annulled-due-to-non-receipt-of-bids-g-kishan-reddy"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"Six years after the CCEA's in-principle nod (2020-10-14, target September 2021) and nearly four years after bids were invited (Dec 2022, per search summaries), NMDC Steel has no strategic buyer; the Rs 23,140-crore Nagarnar plant remains a listed PSU.",whyItMatters:"A privatisation that names no beneficiary is a documented absence: the largest single greenfield steel privatisation in India has found no private capital willing to pay.",srcs:[["PIB PRID 1664359","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1664359"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"The ministry's Tranche IV release reports the 8 successful blocks and the cumulative 22 successes, but not the 11 of 21 offered blocks that did not clear technical evaluation, nor bidder counts per block.",whyItMatters:"Without the denominator (blocks offered, bidders per block) the published success rate cannot be checked and the thinness of competition on the low-premium blocks (c023) cannot be tested.",srcs:[["PIB PRID 2071441","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2071441"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"No public denial or response from Adani Enterprises to NMDC-CMDC's 2023-08-28 termination of the Bailadila Deposit-13 MDO contract; the company did not respond to the Free Press Journal.",whyItMatters:"The contra to an alleged-tier claim is missing by the accused party's choice; it also cuts against the usual 'Adani is favoured in mining' narrative — here a PSU JV terminated the group's only iron-ore MDO.",srcs:[["Free Press Journal, 28 Sep 2023","https://www.freepressjournal.in/india/chhattisgarh-nmdc-cmdc-cancels-iron-ore-mining-contract-with-adani-enterprises"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"The ECI's 2022 opinion on Hemant Soren's disqualification was sent to the Governor of Jharkhand in August 2022 and has never been published or acted on.",whyItMatters:"A constitutional referee's finding on a sitting Chief Minister's self-allotted mining lease sits in a file; neither the accusation nor the exoneration is on the public record, which is a failure of the process rather than a fact about Soren.",srcs:[["Wikipedia: Hemant Soren","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemant_Soren"],["Deccan Herald, 27 Aug 2022","https://www.deccanherald.com/national/east-and-northeast/storm-brewing-for-jharkhand-cm-soren-heres-what-we-know-so-far-1139789.html"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"No consolidated public figure for dividends the Government of India has received from Hindustan Zinc since 2002 appears in the opened sources, even though 'steady dividends' is the government's stated reason for slowing the stake sale.",whyItMatters:"The size of the dividend stream is the number that decides whether holding 27.94% is prudent or a favour to the controlling shareholder's dividend policy; it is not in the public argument.",srcs:[["Outlook Business, 13 Jun 2025","https://www.outlookbusiness.com/corporate/steady-dividends-make-govt-hold-off-on-hindustan-zinc-stake-sale"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"Of Vedanta's Rs 400 crore and Essel Mining's Rs 224.5 crore in bonds, only Rs 40 crore and Rs 174.5 crore respectively are traceable to a party (BJD) in the opened sources; the recipients of the remaining Rs 360 crore and Rs 50 crore are not identified here.",whyItMatters:"Most of the two largest mining donors' money cannot be matched to a recipient from what was opened; the ECI's bond-number matching data would resolve it.",srcs:[["Moneylife, Mar 2024","https://www.moneylife.in/article/electoral-bonds-future-gaming-megha-engineering-qwik-supply-vedanta-haldia-bharti-group-essel-mining-among-top-donors-bjp-encashed-maximum-bonds-worth-rs606051-crore/73697.html"],["Forbes India, 22 Mar 2024","https://www.forbesindia.com/article/news/aditya-birla-group-jindal-steel-and-power-among-largest-buyers-of-electoral-bonds-in-resourcerich-odisha/92215/1"]],domain:"mines"},{what:"Adani group flagship companies do not appear in the ECI purchaser list of 22,217 electoral bonds (Apr 2019–Feb 2024).",whyItMatters:"The group most often alleged to benefit from policy shows no traceable bond money; the graph must not infer funding from proximity. Innocent and alternative readings: (a) bonds were one of several legal channels (trusts, direct cheques, individual purchases); (b) the Adani Foundation gave ₹100 cr to PM CARES in March 2020; (c) purchases by unrelated-name entities are possible but undocumented (compare Qwik/Reliance); (d) the ECI data does not cover Mar 2018–11 Apr 2019.",srcs:[["Frontline (The Hindu group), 15 Mar 2024, 'As ECI reveals electoral bonds data, BJP tops beneficiary list' — reprinted on ADR site","https://adrindia.org/content/eci-reveals-electoral-bonds-data-bjp-tops-beneficiary-list-biggest-donor-little-known-future"],["Indian Express, 29 Mar–1 Apr 2020, 'Here's how India Inc is contributing in fight against coronavirus' (RIL ₹500 cr, Adani Foundation ₹100 cr, SAIL ₹30 cr, Tata ₹1,500 cr, Vedanta pledge ₹100 cr, L&T ₹150 cr)","https://indianexpress.com/article/coronavirus/heres-how-india-inc-is-contributing-in-fight-against-coronavirus-pandemic-6337472/"],["The Hindu Data, 14 Mar 2024, 'SBI electoral bond data: full list of donors and parties' (22,217 bonds bought / 22,030 encashed, 1 Apr 2019–15 Feb 2024)","https://www.thehindu.com/data/sbi-electoral-bond-data-full-list-of-donors-and-parties-which-encashed/article67946737.ece"]],domain:"money"},{what:"Reliance Industries and other Mukesh Ambani flagships are absent from the purchaser list; the third-largest purchaser Qwik Supply Chain (₹410 cr, ₹375 cr to BJP) is 50% owned by three Reliance group companies, and Reliance denies it is a subsidiary.",whyItMatters:"A documented absence at flagship level coexists with a documented associate-level presence; both must be shown. RIL also gave ₹500 cr to PM CARES.",srcs:[["Frontline (The Hindu group), 15 Mar 2024, 'As ECI reveals electoral bonds data, BJP tops beneficiary list' — reprinted on ADR site","https://adrindia.org/content/eci-reveals-electoral-bonds-data-bjp-tops-beneficiary-list-biggest-donor-little-known-future"],["The Hindu Data, 21 Mar 2024, 'Electoral bonds full data | MEIL's ₹584 crore to BJP is top donation to any party' (Future Gaming ₹542 cr to AITC; Qwik; Haldia; Vedanta; Kolkata trio)","https://www.thehindu.com/data/electoral-bond-full-data-santiago-martin-future-542-crore-trinamool/article67977090.ece"],["Indian Express, 29 Mar–1 Apr 2020, 'Here's how India Inc is contributing in fight against coronavirus' (RIL ₹500 cr, Adani Foundation ₹100 cr, SAIL ₹30 cr, Tata ₹1,500 cr, Vedanta pledge ₹100 cr, L&T ₹150 cr)","https://indianexpress.com/article/coronavirus/heres-how-india-inc-is-contributing-in-fight-against-coronavirus-pandemic-6337472/"]],domain:"money"},{what:"Tata group companies are absent from the bond purchaser list, and Tata's Progressive Electoral Trust declared nil receipts for FY2020-21 to FY2023-24 — then received ₹915 cr in FY2024-25 and gave ₹757.6 cr to BJP.",whyItMatters:"The 'Tata gave nothing' reading is true only for the bond channel and only until April 2024; the group is the BJP's largest identified donor of FY25.",srcs:[["ADR — Analysis of Contribution Reports of Electoral Trusts FY 2023-24 (10 Feb 2025, PDF)","https://adrindia.org/sites/default/files/English_Analysis_of_Contribution_reports_of_Electoral_trusts_FY_2023-24.pdf"],["ADR — Analysis of Contribution Reports of Electoral Trusts FY 2024-25 (13 Feb 2026, updated PDF)","https://adrindia.org/sites/default/files/Updated_Eng_Analysis_of_Contribution_reports_of_Electoral_trusts_FY_2024-25_0.pdf"],["Scroll, 27 Nov 2025, 'How Tata Group became BJP's biggest donor weeks after Modi cabinet cleared its semiconductor units' (Progressive Electoral Trust ₹758 cr to BJP, Apr 2024)","https://scroll.in/article/1088771/how-tata-group-became-bjps-biggest-donor-weeks-after-modi-cabinet-cleared-its-semiconductor-units"],["Frontline (The Hindu group), 15 Mar 2024, 'As ECI reveals electoral bonds data, BJP tops beneficiary list' — reprinted on ADR site","https://adrindia.org/content/eci-reveals-electoral-bonds-data-bjp-tops-beneficiary-list-biggest-donor-little-known-future"]],domain:"money"},{what:"The PMO refused, under RTI, to furnish details of contributions to PM CARES, stating the Fund is not a 'public authority' under s.2(h) RTI Act; contributor-level PSU figures exist only because individual PSUs answered RTIs.",whyItMatters:"There is no official contributor list; the ₹2,422.87 cr PSU-CSR figure is a floor assembled from 121 responding PSUs, not a total.",srcs:[["Indian Express, 7 Dec 2020, '101 PSUs give Rs 155 crore from their staff salaries to PM fund' (RTI: 98 PSUs ₹2,422.87 cr CSR; ONGC ₹300 cr, NTPC ₹250 cr, IOC ₹225 cr; PMO refuses RTI)","https://indianexpress.com/article/india/101-psus-give-rs-155-crore-from-their-staff-salaries-to-pm-cares-fund-7094510/"],["Wikipedia — PM CARES Fund (receipts, PSU CSR ₹2,400 cr, MCA circular, RTI status)","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PM_CARES_Fund"]],domain:"money"},{what:"Prudent Electoral Trust did not declare donor addresses for 60 donations worth ₹174.83 cr in FY2023-24; Triumph declared none for ₹132.5 cr; Paribartan converted its ₹1 cr into electoral bonds, hiding the recipient.",whyItMatters:"Trust filings are the post-bond transparency channel, yet ~25% of FY24 trust money cannot be tied to a domicile or (for Paribartan) a party.",srcs:[["ADR — Analysis of Contribution Reports of Electoral Trusts FY 2023-24 (10 Feb 2025, PDF)","https://adrindia.org/sites/default/files/English_Analysis_of_Contribution_reports_of_Electoral_trusts_FY_2023-24.pdf"]],domain:"money"},{what:"AB General Electoral Trust's FY2024-25 donor list had not been published by ECI when ADR and Scroll reported (Feb 2026/Dec 2025), although BJP's report shows ₹621 cr received from it.",whyItMatters:"The Aditya Birla group's post-bond funding — the group behind Essel Mining and Utkal Alumina — is inferred from custom, not filed records.",srcs:[["ADR — Analysis of donations declared by National Parties FY 2024-25 (26 Mar 2026, PDF)","https://adrindia.org/sites/default/files/English_Analysis_of_donations_declared_by_National_Parties_FY_2024-25.pdf"],["Scroll, 22 Dec 2025, 'BJP cornered 85% of political donations last year, up from 56%' (FY2024-25 trust and direct donors: MEIL+Krishna Reddy ₹320 cr, RPSG ₹144 cr, Jindal ₹107 cr, Torrent ₹98.5 cr to Prudent; Rungta ₹95 cr, Vedanta ₹65 cr direct to BJP; Vedanta ₹20 cr to JMM)","https://scroll.in/article/1089471/bjp-cornered-85-of-political-donations-last-year-up-from-56"]],domain:"money"},{what:"Ayodhya/Kashi temple projects and Sangh-linked institutions: no opened source itemises any energy-PSU CSR to them 2019–25. Statue of Unity and PM CARES are now itemised (ThePrint from CSR reports; CAG via Business Standard; PIB/PTI), and the temple-town money found is small: IOC ₹5 cr to the Jagannath temple (FY20), ONGC ~₹1 cr to Gangotri (FY19–20), and a ₹100 cr Badrinath commitment announced May 2021.",whyItMatters:"The 'PSU CSR to temples' narrative is, on the evidence opened, an order of magnitude smaller than PSU CSR to PM CARES (≥₹1,031 cr oil PSUs + ₹925 cr power PSUs in FY20) and to the Statue of Unity (₹146.83 cr in FY17 alone; ≥₹293 cr over five years). If Ayodhya-scale energy-PSU CSR exists it would change that ranking; csr.gov.in project-level data (JS-rendered, not fetchable here) is where it would show.",srcs:[["ThePrint (Remya Nair), 18 Jun 2021, 'Rs 1,355 cr — how much oil PSUs have given temple towns, PM Cares, Statue of Unity as CSR' (from PSU CSR reports FY2014-15→FY2019-20; ONGC response; BPCL/IOCL/GAIL/minister did not respond)","https://theprint.in/economy/rs-1355-cr-how-much-oil-psus-have-given-temple-towns-pm-cares-statue-of-unity-as-csr/677548/"],["Business Standard (Sachin P Mampatta), 31 Oct 2018, 'State-run firms partially funded Sardar Patel's Statue of Unity under CSR' (CAG report for 2016-17: five oil CPSEs ₹146.83 cr to SVPRET; 'not a heritage asset'; ONGC and others' justifications; 12 firms ≥₹293 cr per Prime Database; no company or SVPRET replied)","https://www.business-standard.com/amp/article/current-affairs/psus-may-have-spent-more-on-patel-s-statue-of-unity-than-cag-s-estimate-118103001462_1.html"],["PIB (Ministry of Power), 31 Mar 2020, 'Power Finance Corporation contributes Rs 200 crore under CSR to PM CARES Fund' — Release ID 1609676 (part of ₹925 cr committed by MoP+MNRE PSUs)","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1609676"]],domain:"money"},{what:"Mahi Banswara Nuclear Island Mega EPC Package (>₹28,000 cr) floated 2026-07-15 has no announced winner as of 2026-09-25; the task's premise that 'MEIL or L&T won' is not yet true.",whyItMatters:"It will be the largest nuclear contract in India; the bidder set (MEIL, L&T, BHEL, others) and QCBS scores should be captured when awarded.",srcs:[["Business Standard: ASHVINI floats Rs 28,000 cr nuclear island EPC tender (15 Jul 2026)","https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/ashvini-floats-rs-28000-crore-nuclear-island-epc-tender-126071501436_1.html"],["WNN: Tender set to be launched for Mahi Banswara (15 Jul 2026)","https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/tender-set-to-be-launched-for-mahi-banswara-plant"]],domain:"nuclear"},{what:"No Jaitapur (EDF) construction contract or framework agreement as of 2025-03 (Lok Sabha) despite a binding offer in 2021-04; environmental clearance lapsed 2022-12.",whyItMatters:"Tests the narrative that SHANTI unblocks EDF — nothing signed nine months after assent.",srcs:[["Wikipedia: Jaitapur Nuclear Power Project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaitapur_Nuclear_Power_Project"],["World Nuclear Association: Nuclear Power in India (updated 15 Jul 2026)","https://world-nuclear.org/information-library/country-profiles/countries-g-n/india"]],domain:"nuclear"},{what:"Westinghouse had not submitted a techno-commercial offer for Kovvada as of 2024-12-06; no later offer found.",whyItMatters:"Same test for the US vendor; land (2,079.66 acres) and ~₹1,450 cr of pre-project spending sit idle.",srcs:[["Construction World: Kovvada talks with Westinghouse (Lok Sabha reply 6 Dec 2024)","https://www.constructionworld.in/energy-infrastructure/power-and-renewable-energy/india-advances-kovvada-nuclear-project-talks-with-westinghouse/66201"]],domain